From 7c70cc2278a9ae31e47fc2c66a19902b6463b2b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan <kloterstefan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:57:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] SEQ MIDI OUT on Skiff 2.0's sequencer: notes, step
 position, clock, start/stop over USB MIDI

Vizz 1.0's SEQ MIDI OUT (patches 0001, 0002 on Skiff 1.4) ported to the
sequencer of Skiff 2.0: each track plays out on its MIDI channel (T1..T6
CHANNEL), notes and drum hits with velocity (accent 127), ratchets,
flams and slides as played; CC 102 = step index on entering a step;
MIDI Clock (24 ppq), Start and Stop with the INT clock; CC 123 when a
panic drops what was sent sounding (MIDI IN overflow, CC 120 received).
MENU > MIDI > SEQ MIDI OUT (ON by default; bit 3 of the settings byte
CPU2_BYTE, as Vizz 1.0 kept it).

What 2.0 adds, as the sequencer does it (seq_step, seq_keep_only,
seq_gate_end, launch_swap):
- a note of its own length (NOTES' LENGTH: per-note ties, a GATE lock)
  ends with its own note-off, a chord's notes apart; a tie is one note
- MIDI has one note of a pitch on a channel: one struck again while it
  still sounds there ends first (seq_mo: the notes sent sounding)
- a chain's parts: CC 102 counts each from its own step 0; a note going
  on from one part into the next is one note
- SONG ONCE's end stops the transport (seq_stop): note-offs and Stop

tests/seqmidi_test.c: Vizz 1.0's cases on 2.0 and the new ones
(lengths, overlap, ties, chain, SONG ONCE, every pitch's on / off
alternating). ui_test, feat13_test: the MIDI tab has eleven rows; the
FX key test counts the key's MIDI alone. tests/ui_golden.txt: the MIDI
tab's two pictures (its first rows, scrolled to T6) in every palette,
28 of 3388, with the new row; no other picture changes.

